  "market_context": "Bearish market structure confirmed by series of lower highs and lower lows on GBP/JPY 1H chart. Price formed a consolidation area, then faked out upward before returning inside, indicating selling pressure and continuation of downtrend.",
  "key_observation": "Price broke above a consolidation zone (fake-out) but quickly returned inside it, signaling strong selling pressure and a high-probability short entry after candle close back inside the zone.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a clear downtrend on GBP/JPY 1H using lower highs and lower lows as structural confirmation.",
    "Step 2: Observed a consolidation area forming within the downtrend, acting as resistance.",
    "Step 3: Noted price breaking above the consolidation (fake-out) to the upside, triggering liquidity above the zone.",
    "Step 4: Waited for price to return and close back inside the consolidation area, confirming rejection of the breakout and bearish continuation.",
    "Step 5: Placed short entry after the candle closed inside the consolidation, with stop-loss above the swing high that formed during the fake-out."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Fake-outs above consolidation zones in a confirmed downtrend often signal institutional selling; entering after price closes back inside the zone offers high-probability short setups with defined risk above the swing high.",
